                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_458">Reading,
                                Berkshire, Benedictine abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was accepted (with a query) in the second edition of
                                Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). However, it was later
                                rejected in the Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain index card records the following
                                information, which was ultimately deemed unsatisfactory for an
                                attribution:</p><p>Lacks fol. 1. Phillipps catalogue says <q>Ex
                                    Bibl. Abbatiae de Reading.</q> De Ricci, <title>Census</title>,
                                I, 1035, says <q>probably from Reading Abbey</q> - assumption based
                                on J. Bowen's ownership.</p></provenance>
